#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:2 90414304b2224d2abe71757a2ffda5a0
msgid "Creating a library by being asked"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:4 1e3eb041a5a6407baf6304ec0cd1ddfe
msgid ""
"``mhvtl library create --interactive`` walks through the same choices the"
" form does, one question at a time, offering only what the vendor's "
"catalogue allows for the answers so far."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:8 96d27818a3da420b987364ea62039e3a
msgid ""
"It is the terminal equivalent of the form rather than a shortcut: use it "
"when you do not already know which model takes which drive, or when you "
"want to see what the options *are* before committing to any of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:12 7ebc937c78564d579edb067f23e167d4
msgid ""
"**Nothing is written until the last answer.** Ctrl-C at any point, or "
"``q`` at the end, leaves the host exactly as it was."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:20 621d71af8fa04169b5e54955c4e3bd5e
msgid "The whole thing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:80 5a423eefde7b492fb0286501e9a3766c
msgid ""
"Every answer above was left empty except the first, so the whole library "
"is IBM's defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:84 0963af910c7f40059c1e064cb3716cbe
msgid "Each list is only what is still possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:86 110369925d084dcbb528cbefb5edec2b
msgid ""
"The questions narrow as they go, and that is the point of asking them in "
"this order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:89 d642b9f4a6fb436392badf2910e37b68
msgid ""
"Answer ``IBM`` and the **library model** list is IBM's thirteen models. "
"Answer ``03584L32`` and the **drive model** list is the fourteen drives "
"*that model* takes - the LTO line. Had you chosen ``03584L22`` instead, "
"the same question would have offered four 3592 drives and no LTO drive at"
" all, because that is a 3592 library. Choose ``03584L42`` and it offers "
"two DLT drives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:95 075bc15aa431414994db6ab93ef644fc
msgid ""
"Then the **cartridge density** list is only what the drive you picked can"
" write. An ULT3580-TD8 offers LTO8 and LTO7; an ULT3580-TDA offers LTO10 "
"and LTO10P."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:99 587b66cdbc4d4c9eb6983eda9d050b39
msgid ""
"So a combination the vendor does not make is not refused at the end - it "
"is never offered. There is no way to answer these questions wrongly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:103
#: 978ff4eeb8c74ca3ad72657d4d256cd2
msgid "Two limits it tells you about"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:105
#: 854572d18f3b459ba10f684d082f3994
msgid ""
"``71 drive(s) at most here, limited by SCSI targets`` is not the model's "
"limit, which is 511 for an 03584L32. It is how many drives will still fit"
" on this host beside the libraries already configured. The number changes"
" as you add libraries, which is why it is printed rather than documented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:110
#: b567747e1d4c467880a416c94a6cd5ec
msgid ""
"``Empty slots [4]`` defaults to four, and the summary spells out what "
"that means - ``slots 54 (50 full, 4 empty)`` - because a library with no "
"empty slots cannot take a new cartridge without being reconfigured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:115
#: 3126bc9181c64f788e210b9de487e0fe
msgid "More than one kind of drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:117
#: a252f376150147b3b0e66393992f0f72
msgid ""
"**Add another drive type?** and **Add another density?** are where a "
"mixed library comes from. Answer ``y`` and it asks the same two questions"
" again, and keeps asking until you say no. The order you answer in is the"
" order the drives are given slots, which is also their SCSI target order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:122
#: 3be92495648e44deb9bf4bd0bcafd823
msgid "See :doc:`drives` for what a mixed library is for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:125
#: 1ac86f084b144a7b86aeec63542ffa6c
msgid "The four ways out"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:128
#: ffb9cb24ce8748948ee23320209bef50
msgid "Answer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:128
#: 392de6ef0a6441edb813fa19547d3e71
msgid "What happens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:130
#: 9a134e83ec4f47c2855df95a76826e7b
msgid "``c``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:130
#: 81961f4d6ec04df3bfa066d54098a21b
msgid ""
"Creates it. The same steps the one-shot command reports: validate, "
"create, restart, verify, media."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:132
#: dc9cbf3863ea495cbdd355fe6888260a
msgid "``s``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:132
#: 99bfb4ad2d024716ac7a72a5e109fe7b
msgid ""
"Creates it, then asks for a name and writes the configuration to "
"``presets.toml`` - the same as ``--save-preset NAME``. See :doc"
":`profiles-and-presets`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:136
#: 0c5ef4011fbe48aa94f53b99e55fae19
msgid "``p``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:136
#: 2882f9fc35ef4429961a4e60b200a37f
msgid ""
"Prints the ``device.conf`` text it *would* write, and comes back to this "
"menu. Nothing is written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:138
#: 9d9cce13e72e45f29600ba15f9b50dd5
msgid "``q``, or Ctrl-C"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:138
#: f581c6b49f8a40de98fe7dd4cd71487f
msgid "Quits. ``Nothing was written.``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:141
#: fb8568c89cb64d598a353e619839ea29
msgid ""
"``p`` is worth using the first time. It shows the library stanza and one "
"stanza per drive, with the serial numbers, the SCSI targets and the "
"revision levels the profile chose - which is the detail a backup "
"application will identify the hardware by."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:147
#: 11fd160ea29d445e8030c79730caa722
msgid "The same thing without the questions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:149
#: ccd0cfbb9b1b44cc98b5f2d94b9fe969
msgid ""
"``--dry-run`` on an ordinary create prints that same ``device.conf`` and "
"stops, so you can see the outcome of a command you already know how to "
"type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:172
#: babcd23572664d258f253bcf814637b2
msgid "It reads the configuration but writes nothing, so it needs no privileges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:175
#: bf2c1c40952e464e8ac3f79f61c2199e
msgid "In a script, give the values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:177
#: 4ea6b2d71dbd42738bb01d1c536866ff
msgid ""
"``--interactive`` needs a terminal, and says so rather than hanging or "
"reading nothing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create-interactively.rst:189
#: 4d94e2df88a9410a8d5ae70992a0dab7
msgid ""
":doc:`create` for the form and the one-shot command, and :doc:`profiles-"
"and-presets` for keeping a configuration you have proved."
msgstr ""

